{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhSEVLdU173NefVCp8pb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the 8 test statistics for the `local_representativeness` model into `iter_0/critique/test_stats/`. Each one returns a finite number on the observed data and takes about 0.01 s or less per call, well under the time limit. I haven't run the posterior-predictive check; the pipeline does that.\n\nThe data: 40 participants, each seeing the same 64 pairs (2,560 trials). The model pools everyone, with one shared beta, one side bias and the same feature weights for every length.\n\n| Statistic | What it tests | Observed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `participant_majority_agreement_sd` | Whether people differ in how often they pick the majority's choice by more than a single pooled model allows | 0.149 |\n| `participant_left_rate_sd` | Whether people's left/right biases vary more than one shared side bias allows | 0.078 |\n| `shorter_longest_run_choice` | How often people pick the sequence with the shorter longest streak (the model has no streak feature) | 0.831 |\n| `more_distinct_triplets_choice` | How often people pick the sequence with more distinct 3-flip patterns | 0.690 |\n| `balanced_pairs_more_alternation_choice` | How often people pick the more-alternating sequence when head counts differ by at most one | 0.703 |\n| `length8_minus_short_extremity` | Whether how strongly people agree on a pair depends on sequence length (the model uses one beta for all lengths) | −0.100 |\n| `late_minus_early_majority_agreement` | Whether answers get noisier later in the session, which a fixed model can't produce | 0.009 |\n| `ends_with_repeat_choice` | How often people pick the sequence that ends with two equal flips (the model ignores where flips occur) | 0.183 |\n\n- **Change to the alternation statistic:** I first wrote it for pairs with exactly equal head counts, but no pair in this design has equal head counts. It now uses pairs whose head counts differ by at most one (880 trials).\n- **Short sequences are rare:** 2,040 of the 2,560 trials are length-8 pairs. The length comparison therefore rests on a small set of shorter pairs: 400 trials at length 7 and 120 at lengths 3 and 5."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":49019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":934,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c976e759-752c-47ce-8760-ba31df71cc2b","uuid":"f2fdb33c-5c90-4a97-b992-bd138907d137","timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:30:12.157Z","request_id":"req_011CfhSEUvaJxKu4yEsAUpMW"}
